Saturday morning means my volunteer time at the cafe.
I reach the café in the morning.
Sunita is already there.
There is a lot of rush in the cafe on Saturday mornings.
I put on my apron and start the work.
Sunita makes the coffee, and I prepare the warm sandwiches.
"Maya, give these two coffees to table number four," Sunita tells me.
I immediately take the coffee tray and go to that table.
A regular customer is sitting there.
"Kaka, here is your coffee and warm sandwich," I give it to him with a smile.
He smiles and thanks me.
In a short while, the morning breakfast rush lessens.
Then Sunita and I together clean the counter.
"Maya, you manage all the tasks well now," Sunita says.
We both chat for a while and drink coffee.
This morning the café is bustling.
Tai introduces me to the new customers.
